  "title": "Charter Frontier",
  "rules": [
    "Move on public floor; walls block movement. The middle corridor gate allows entry only during an active charter; upper and lower detours remain open.",
    "Claim at most one plot from distance at most one; ties resolve by lower actor index, then lower plot index. Build there for two materials.",
    "Buildings mature automatically to three. An adjacent owner can collect a mature harvest; each plot needs two collections for joint completion.",
    "Donate one material voluntarily at the council. The public fund holds at most four; donations are not refunded. No agent is forced to donate.",
    "At the council, propose when at least two fund units exist and no ballot, delay or lease is active. Lowest-index proposer wins and starts with yes.",
    "Four subsequent ballot ticks permit remote public yes, no or abstain changes. Only at deadline do at least three yes votes spend two fund units.",
    "A passed charter waits two further transitions, then opens gate entry for twelve ticks. Expiry blocks new entry; an occupant may leave. No automatic eviction.",
    "No single veto rule exists: a no vote is not yes, and two non-yes votes defeat quorum. Failed ballots expire without spending fund."
  ],
